// Audit 2026-10-03 finding 5, second half: a `Scriptor` member that collides
// with a name the module declares.
//
// A prelude capability-bearing receiver -- `Scriptor` here -- has its own
// prelude rows for members and nothing else. `a` and `descriptor` are its
// FIELDS, not rows, so `s.a` and `s.a()` are `EXS-E0305`; and so they must stay
// when the module happens to declare an `interfacies` member of the same name,
// as `Gx` does below. The checker's last-resort lookup -- pass 1's unique
// module-wide member of a name -- used to bind them to `Gx::a` and
// `Gx::descriptor` once the field rows were taken out of `Scriptor`'s lookup:
// the CALL form then typed and reached a lowering that trapped on it: `exsc`
// died on SIGILL, exit 132, where the field rows had given a clean refusal.
// (The READ form was a stray exit 4 from the emitter, never a diagnostic.) A
// fix that only removes rows reintroduces exactly that; a CLOSED SET for the
// receiver does not.
//
// `exsc-exit=1` is a diagnostic's exit status and 132 is the trap; the code is
// pinned one layer down, tests/unit/chk_directorium.asm rows 31-34. The
// differential phase holds `--emitte c` to the same status.

interfacies Gx {
    functio a(self: Scriptor) -> u8
    functio descriptor(self: Scriptor) -> u8
}

publica functio initium(m: Mundus) -> u8 {
    firma a = m.ambitus();
    firma s = Scriptor.ad_exitum(a);
    firma x = s.a;
    firma y = s.descriptor;
    firma c = s.a();
    firma d = s.descriptor();
    redde 0;
}
